1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,454
A customer types your address,

2
00:00:02,454 --> 00:00:03,692
and a page appears.

3
00:00:03,692 --> 00:00:04,539
Who answered?

4
00:00:04,539 --> 00:00:05,385
Not your app.

5
00:00:05,385 --> 00:00:05,776
Often,

6
00:00:05,776 --> 00:00:07,014
it is a web server,

7
00:00:07,014 --> 00:00:09,945
a small program whose whole job is to answer,

8
00:00:09,945 --> 00:00:10,271
fast.

9
00:00:10,821 --> 00:00:14,370
Today you meet the most popular one in the world: engine X.

10
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:15,272
You install it,

11
00:00:15,272 --> 00:00:16,475
you read its config,

12
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:17,257
you break it,

13
00:00:17,257 --> 00:00:18,159
and you fix it.

14
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:19,351
By the end,

15
00:00:19,351 --> 00:00:20,925
you will serve a real page,

16
00:00:20,925 --> 00:00:22,616
show a friendly four oh four,

17
00:00:22,616 --> 00:00:24,832
and hide a detail that attackers love.

18
00:00:25,382 --> 00:00:27,025
Serve it, test it, reload it.

19
00:00:28,575 --> 00:00:31,647
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

20
00:00:32,197 --> 00:00:34,535
One: three roles that people mix up.

21
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:35,379
A web server,

22
00:00:35,379 --> 00:00:36,418
a reverse proxy,

23
00:00:36,418 --> 00:00:38,106
and an application server.

24
00:00:38,656 --> 00:00:44,075
Two: a live demo. We read a real config, and the test tells us exactly what is wrong.

25
00:00:44,625 --> 00:00:45,787
Three: we fix it,

26
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:46,812
start engine X,

27
00:00:46,812 --> 00:00:49,136
and ask for pages like a customer,

28
00:00:49,136 --> 00:00:51,665
including a page that does not exist.

29
00:00:52,215 --> 00:00:53,991
Four: we improve the config,

30
00:00:53,991 --> 00:00:55,704
and apply it with a reload,

31
00:00:55,704 --> 00:00:56,783
with no downtime.

32
00:00:56,783 --> 00:00:57,734
Then your turn,

33
00:00:57,734 --> 00:00:59,447
with a lab that judges you.

34
00:00:59,997 --> 00:01:05,608
This is lesson one of the web servers domain. Next, we point engine X at a real backend.

35
00:01:06,158 --> 00:01:07,566
Serve, test, reload.

36
00:01:09,616 --> 00:01:13,691
Three roles, three jobs. People mix them up, so let us separate them.

37
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:17,020
A web server answers requests with files.

38
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:17,495
A page,

39
00:01:17,495 --> 00:01:18,173
a picture,

40
00:01:18,173 --> 00:01:19,122
a style sheet.

41
00:01:19,122 --> 00:01:20,884
It does not run your code.

42
00:01:20,884 --> 00:01:23,528
It reads a file from disk and sends it.

43
00:01:23,528 --> 00:01:25,087
That is static serving,

44
00:01:25,087 --> 00:01:26,443
and it is very fast.

45
00:01:26,993 --> 00:01:30,283
A reverse proxy answers on behalf of another server.

46
00:01:30,283 --> 00:01:32,307
The customer talks to the proxy.

47
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:34,078
The proxy talks to your app,

48
00:01:34,078 --> 00:01:35,786
and passes the answer back.

49
00:01:35,786 --> 00:01:37,873
The customer never sees your app.

50
00:01:38,423 --> 00:01:40,938
An application server runs your code.

51
00:01:40,938 --> 00:01:41,889
Tomcat is one.

52
00:01:41,889 --> 00:01:43,384
It builds each answer,

53
00:01:43,384 --> 00:01:45,762
from a database and business rules.

54
00:01:45,762 --> 00:01:46,781
It is powerful,

55
00:01:46,781 --> 00:01:47,597
and heavier.

56
00:01:48,147 --> 00:01:49,876
Engine X is a web server,

57
00:01:49,876 --> 00:01:51,952
and a very good reverse proxy.

58
00:01:51,952 --> 00:01:53,266
In front of Tomcat,

59
00:01:53,266 --> 00:01:55,480
it serves the easy files itself,

60
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,971
and forwards only the hard requests.

61
00:01:57,971 --> 00:02:00,669
Today we do the first job: serve files.

62
00:02:02,219 --> 00:02:07,147
Go to the lab folder.

63
00:02:08,697 --> 00:02:10,596
Look around. Type: L S.

64
00:02:11,146 --> 00:02:13,329
Our site is in the site folder.

65
00:02:13,329 --> 00:02:15,582
The config is engine X dot conf.

66
00:02:15,582 --> 00:02:17,061
Logs will go in logs.

67
00:02:17,061 --> 00:02:21,215
And mime dot types tells engine X which file kind is which.

68
00:02:21,765 --> 00:02:25,648
Read the config.

69
00:02:26,198 --> 00:02:27,666
Read it from the top.

70
00:02:27,666 --> 00:02:28,855
Worker processes,

71
00:02:28,855 --> 00:02:29,765
a P I D file,

72
00:02:29,765 --> 00:02:30,534
and events.

73
00:02:30,534 --> 00:02:31,933
Then the http block,

74
00:02:31,933 --> 00:02:32,562
our logs,

75
00:02:32,562 --> 00:02:33,821
some temp folders,

76
00:02:33,821 --> 00:02:35,290
and one server block.

77
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:39,277
That server block is the heart of it: listen is the port,

78
00:02:39,277 --> 00:02:41,515
and root is the folder of files.

79
00:02:42,065 --> 00:02:50,342
Test the config before you start.

80
00:02:50,892 --> 00:02:51,503
It fails,

81
00:02:51,503 --> 00:02:53,536
and it tells us exactly where.

82
00:02:53,536 --> 00:02:55,231
Emerg means an emergency.

83
00:02:55,231 --> 00:02:56,791
Invalid parameter root,

84
00:02:56,791 --> 00:02:57,943
in the conf file,

85
00:02:57,943 --> 00:02:58,893
line fourteen.

86
00:02:58,893 --> 00:03:00,791
Always read the line number.

87
00:03:01,341 --> 00:03:05,544
Open the file in vim.

88
00:03:06,094 --> 00:03:07,770
Line fourteen says root,

89
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:10,774
but the real mistake is the line before it.

90
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:13,218
Listen has no semicolon at the end.

91
00:03:13,218 --> 00:03:16,571
Every setting in engine X ends with a semicolon.

92
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:17,968
Go to line thirteen,

93
00:03:17,968 --> 00:03:18,457
add it,

94
00:03:18,457 --> 00:03:19,086
and save.

95
00:03:21,136 --> 00:03:23,760
Test again.

96
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:28,854
Syntax is ok, and the test is successful. Now it is safe to start.

97
00:03:29,404 --> 00:03:31,772
Start nginx.

98
00:03:32,322 --> 00:03:34,050
No output means it started.

99
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:40,829
Is it listening?

100
00:03:41,379 --> 00:03:44,024
Yes: listening, on port eighty-one eighty-one.

101
00:03:44,574 --> 00:03:52,318
Ask for the headers.

102
00:03:52,868 --> 00:03:53,673
Two hundred,

103
00:03:53,673 --> 00:03:53,874
OK.

104
00:03:53,874 --> 00:03:55,147
The page was found.

105
00:03:55,147 --> 00:03:58,767
Look at the server line: it says the engine X version,

106
00:03:58,767 --> 00:04:00,777
and even the operating system.

107
00:04:00,777 --> 00:04:02,319
We will hide that soon.

108
00:04:02,869 --> 00:04:08,586
Ask for the page.

109
00:04:09,136 --> 00:04:13,424
Welcome to CloudCart. Served by engine X, straight from a folder.

110
00:04:13,974 --> 00:04:23,340
Ask for a page that does not exist.

111
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:24,734
Four oh four,

112
00:04:24,734 --> 00:04:25,383
not found.

113
00:04:25,383 --> 00:04:26,422
That is correct.

114
00:04:26,422 --> 00:04:30,188
But the page a customer would see is a plain gray default.

115
00:04:30,188 --> 00:04:31,292
We can do better.

116
00:04:31,842 --> 00:04:35,917
Improve the config.

117
00:04:36,467 --> 00:04:37,172
Two lines.

118
00:04:37,172 --> 00:04:38,863
Inside the server block,

119
00:04:38,863 --> 00:04:40,554
error page four oh four,

120
00:04:40,554 --> 00:04:42,316
pointing to our own page.

121
00:04:42,316 --> 00:04:43,866
And in the http block,

122
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:45,134
server tokens off,

123
00:04:45,134 --> 00:04:46,825
which hides the version.

124
00:04:46,825 --> 00:04:47,459
Add them,

125
00:04:47,459 --> 00:04:48,094
and save.

126
00:04:58,144 --> 00:05:05,632
Test, then reload.

127
00:05:06,182 --> 00:05:08,162
Reload applies the new config,

128
00:05:08,162 --> 00:05:09,283
without stopping.

129
00:05:09,283 --> 00:05:10,801
Customers never notice.

130
00:05:10,801 --> 00:05:14,563
That is the safe way to change a live server: test first,

131
00:05:14,563 --> 00:05:15,355
then reload.

132
00:05:15,905 --> 00:05:23,073
Ask for the missing page again.

133
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:24,537
Page not found,

134
00:05:24,537 --> 00:05:25,573
in our own style,

135
00:05:25,573 --> 00:05:26,914
with a link back home.

136
00:05:26,914 --> 00:05:28,194
Still a four oh four,

137
00:05:28,194 --> 00:05:29,170
only friendlier.

138
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:36,653
Is the version hidden?

139
00:05:37,203 --> 00:05:42,344
Just engine X. No version number. A small secure default, and an easy win.

140
00:05:42,894 --> 00:05:49,721
Every request is written down.

141
00:05:50,271 --> 00:05:50,888
Who asked,

142
00:05:50,888 --> 00:05:51,197
when,

143
00:05:51,197 --> 00:05:51,506
what,

144
00:05:51,506 --> 00:05:52,740
and the answer code.

145
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:56,074
We will read these like a detective in a later lesson.

146
00:05:56,624 --> 00:05:58,992
Run the judge.

147
00:05:59,542 --> 00:06:00,345
Five checks,

148
00:06:00,345 --> 00:06:01,148
five passes.

149
00:06:01,148 --> 00:06:02,018
Config valid,

150
00:06:02,018 --> 00:06:03,155
engine X running,

151
00:06:03,155 --> 00:06:04,226
the page served,

152
00:06:04,226 --> 00:06:05,832
a friendly four oh four,

153
00:06:05,832 --> 00:06:07,371
and the version hidden.

154
00:06:07,921 --> 00:06:09,884
Clean up.

155
00:06:10,434 --> 00:06:12,823
Engine X stopped, and everything removed.

156
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:17,896
Is the port free? Count the lines.

157
00:06:18,446 --> 00:06:21,454
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind.

158
00:06:23,004 --> 00:06:25,863
Your task. Serve a static site with engine X.

159
00:06:26,413 --> 00:06:32,343
One: lab up, then N G dash T. It fails. Read the line number, and fix the config in vim.

160
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:37,608
Two: test again until it succeeds. Then start engine X, and curl the page.

161
00:06:38,158 --> 00:06:42,766
Three: add error page four oh four, so a missing page shows your friendly page.

162
00:06:43,316 --> 00:06:46,196
Four: add server tokens off, to hide the version.

163
00:06:46,746 --> 00:06:50,245
Five: test, then reload. Then lab check, and lab down.

164
00:06:52,295 --> 00:06:56,071
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen, and write it down.

165
00:06:56,621 --> 00:06:58,269
The lab lives on GitHub,

166
00:06:58,269 --> 00:06:59,436
at it dash waves,

167
00:06:59,436 --> 00:07:01,016
slash dev ops dash A I,

168
00:07:01,016 --> 00:07:02,526
in the folder academy,

169
00:07:02,526 --> 00:07:03,213
slash lab.

170
00:07:03,763 --> 00:07:09,075
Two files: lab one eighteen dot S H, and shortcuts one eighteen dot S H.

171
00:07:09,625 --> 00:07:10,530
Install it,

172
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:13,410
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

173
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:15,303
dash m seven five five,

174
00:07:15,303 --> 00:07:17,360
lab one eighteen dot S H,

175
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,594
into slash usr,

176
00:07:18,594 --> 00:07:19,582
slash local,

177
00:07:19,582 --> 00:07:20,569
slash S bin.

178
00:07:21,119 --> 00:07:25,649
Load the short names with: source shortcuts one eighteen dot S H.

179
00:07:25,649 --> 00:07:26,833
You get two: lab,

180
00:07:26,833 --> 00:07:27,391
and N G.

181
00:07:27,941 --> 00:07:30,294
You need engine X and curl installed,

182
00:07:30,294 --> 00:07:32,583
and port eighty-one eighty-one free.

183
00:07:32,583 --> 00:07:34,999
The lab runs its own private engine X,

184
00:07:34,999 --> 00:07:37,797
so it does not touch the one on your system.

185
00:07:38,347 --> 00:07:40,054
Lab up prepares everything.

186
00:07:40,054 --> 00:07:41,761
Lab check judges your work.

187
00:07:41,761 --> 00:07:43,278
Lab down removes it all.

188
00:07:43,278 --> 00:07:45,302
Only run it on your own machine.

189
00:07:47,352 --> 00:07:49,421
Pass or fail. You need all five.

190
00:07:49,971 --> 00:07:51,571
The config passes the test.

191
00:07:52,121 --> 00:07:54,703
Engine X is running and answers on its port.

192
00:07:55,253 --> 00:07:56,981
The CloudCart page is served.

193
00:07:57,531 --> 00:08:00,816
A missing page gives a four oh four, with your friendly page.

194
00:08:01,366 --> 00:08:03,222
The server header hides the version.

195
00:08:03,772 --> 00:08:05,073
To pass, all five.

196
00:08:07,123 --> 00:08:08,894
Your turn, on your own machine.

197
00:08:09,444 --> 00:08:13,774
One: lab up, read the task list, and run N G dash T. Read the error.

198
00:08:14,324 --> 00:08:17,247
Two: fix the semicolon in vim, and test again.

199
00:08:17,797 --> 00:08:22,170
Three: start engine X, and ask for the page, and for a page that is missing.

200
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:26,560
Four: add error page and server tokens off, test, and reload.

201
00:08:27,110 --> 00:08:30,268
Five: run lab check until you see five out of five.

202
00:08:30,818 --> 00:08:33,399
Six: lab down, and prove the port is free.

203
00:08:33,949 --> 00:08:35,784
Pause the video, and begin now.

204
00:08:51,334 --> 00:08:52,209
Quick check.

205
00:08:52,759 --> 00:08:56,279
What is the difference between a web server and an application server?

206
00:08:56,829 --> 00:08:59,175
Why do you test the config before you reload?

207
00:08:59,725 --> 00:09:03,352
What does a four oh four mean, and who decides what the customer sees?

208
00:09:03,902 --> 00:09:05,481
Why hide the server version?

209
00:09:06,031 --> 00:09:08,382
Objectives covered: M C thirteen,

210
00:09:08,382 --> 00:09:10,020
objectives one and two.

211
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,160
The three roles,

212
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:14,009
and installing and configuring engine X.

213
00:09:14,559 --> 00:09:16,629
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

214
